	)
	(text "Li-Polymer Charge Management Controller"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 122.428 36.576 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ee9f894f-0e5c-481c-8a3b-f8acd41165e8")
	)
	(text "1- First, let's calculate RHOT and RCOLD:\nNTC thermistor of 10kΩ at 25°C(298.15K) with β = 3800K\nTemperature range: 0°C(273.15K) to 50°C(323.15K)\nUsing the B-parameter equation: R = R25 × e^[β(1/T - 1/T25)]:\nRCOLD(At 0°C) = 10k × e^[3800 × (1/273.15 - 1/298.15)] ≈ 32.1kΩ\nRHOT(At 50°C) = 10k × e^[3800 × (1/323.15 - 1/298.15)] ≈ 3.73kΩ\n\n2- Calculate RT1 and RT2\n24kΩ = RT1 + (RT2 × RCOLD)/(RT2 + RCOLD)   [Equation 1]\n5kΩ = RT1 + (RT2 × RHOT)/(RT2 + RHOT)      [Equation 2]\nWe can solve it numerically or iteratively:\nLet's assume RT2 is much larger than RHOT (e.g., RT2≫3.73kΩ).\nFrom Equation 2: 5kΩ≈RT1+3.73kΩ => RT1≈5kΩ−3.73kΩ=1.27kΩ\nSubstitute RT1=1.27kΩ into Equation 1 and solve it!\nThis gives us:\nRT1 ≈ 1.27kΩ (use a standard value of 1.3kΩ)\nRT2 ≈ 77.9kΩ (use a standard value of 78kΩ or 75kΩ)\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.834 96.774 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f4a704c9-efe3-4dc5-9dfa-cfa51c403c8e")
	)
